damaged_code:
```rust
fn process_url(untrusted_url: String) {
    let validated_url = sanitize(&untrusted_url);
    fetch_page(&validated_url);
}
```

counterexample:
Variables with descriptive names representing domain semantic differences without security state transitions:
```rust
let home_address: String = ...;
let work_address: String = ...;
```

fix:
Represent the transition via strongly typed wrappers that make it impossible to bypass sanitization.
```rust
struct UntrustedUrl(String);
struct SafeUrl(String);

fn sanitize(input: UntrustedUrl) -> SafeUrl { ... }
fn fetch_page(url: SafeUrl) { ... }
```
